    <title>Data &amp; Compute Trade-offs:
  When Do Larger Models Stop Paying Off?</title>
    <summary>We show that loss &lt; 2.0 nats is reached sooner by scaling data than by
scaling parameters once compute exceeds 10^22 FLOPs, and we discuss the
&quot;data wall&quot; for language models &amp; vision models.</summary>
